{
  "datasets": [
    {
      "name": "kpis",
      "displayName": "kpis",
      "queryLines": [
        "SELECT\n",
        "  (SELECT count_if(is_down) FROM gold_site_status) AS sites_down,\n",
        "  (SELECT sum(IF(is_down, subscribers_served, 0)) FROM gold_site_status) AS subscribers_on_down_sites,\n",
        "  (SELECT round(100 * avg(IF(is_down, 0, 1)), 2) FROM gold_site_status) AS sites_in_service_pct,\n",
        "  (SELECT count(*) FROM silver_alarms WHERE raised_ts > (SELECT max(raised_ts) FROM silver_alarms) - INTERVAL 24 HOURS) AS alarms_24h,\n",
        "  (SELECT count(*) FROM noc_incidents) AS open_incidents,\n",
        "  (SELECT count(*) FROM noc_incidents WHERE incident_type = 'kpi_anomaly') AS silent_degradations\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "network_hourly",
      "displayName": "network hourly",
      "queryLines": [
        "SELECT ts, market, availability_pct, alarms_raised, sites_down, drop_call_rate_pct\nFROM gold_network_hourly\nWHERE ts > (SELECT max(ts) FROM gold_network_hourly) - INTERVAL 36 HOURS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "router_status",
      "displayName": "router status",
      "queryLines": [
        "WITH r AS (\n  SELECT agg_router_id, count_if(is_down) AS down_cnt, count_if(NOT is_down) AS up_cnt, count(*) AS tot\n  FROM gold_site_status GROUP BY agg_router_id\n)\nSELECT agg_router_id, 'down' AS status, down_cnt AS sites FROM r\nUNION ALL\nSELECT agg_router_id, 'up' AS status, up_cnt AS sites FROM r"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "incidents",
      "displayName": "incidents",
      "queryLines": [
        "SELECT incident_id, suggested_priority AS priority, incident_type, title, market, CAST(detected_ts AS STRING) AS detected, sites_affected, subscribers_served, alarm_count, active_alarms\n",
        "FROM noc_incidents ORDER BY suggested_priority, detected_ts DESC\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "top_anomalies",
      "displayName": "top anomalies",
      "queryLines": [
        "SELECT cell_id, CAST(day AS STRING) AS day, anomaly_score, array_join(top_factors, ' · ') AS why_flagged\n",
        "FROM cell_health_daily WHERE is_anomaly AND day >= (SELECT date_sub(max(day), 1) FROM cell_health_daily)\n",
        "QUALIFY row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY cell_id ORDER BY anomaly_score DESC) = 1 ORDER BY anomaly_score DESC LIMIT 10\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "slow_burn",
      "displayName": "slow burn",
      "queryLines": [
        "WITH top AS (SELECT cell_id FROM cell_health_daily WHERE is_anomaly GROUP BY cell_id ORDER BY max(drop_call_rate_pct - baseline_drop_call_rate_pct) DESC LIMIT 1)\n",
        "SELECT k.day, k.cell_id, k.drop_call_rate_pct, k.max_vswr FROM gold_cell_kpi_daily k\n",
        "WHERE k.site_id IN (SELECT substring(cell_id, 1, 7) FROM top)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "mttr",
      "displayName": "mttr",
      "queryLines": [
        "SELECT CASE category WHEN 'congestion' THEN 'Congestion' WHEN 'fiber_cut' THEN 'Fiber cut' WHEN 'interference' THEN 'Interference' WHEN 'microwave' THEN 'Microwave' WHEN 'optics_degradation' THEN 'Optics degradation' WHEN 'planned_work_overrun' THEN 'Planned work overrun' WHEN 'power' THEN 'Power' WHEN 'rf_hardware' THEN 'RF hardware' WHEN 'software' THEN 'Software' ELSE category END AS category_label, count(*) AS tickets, round(avg(mttr_hours), 1) AS avg_mttr_hours ",
        "FROM trouble_tickets ",
        "WHERE opened_ts >= add_months((SELECT max(opened_ts) FROM trouble_tickets), -12) ",
        "GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY avg_mttr_hours DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "early_warning",
      "displayName": "early warning",
      "queryLines": [
        "SELECT CASE category WHEN 'congestion' THEN 'Congestion' WHEN 'fiber_cut' THEN 'Fiber cut' WHEN 'interference' THEN 'Interference' WHEN 'microwave' THEN 'Microwave' WHEN 'optics_degradation' THEN 'Optics degradation' WHEN 'planned_work_overrun' THEN 'Planned work overrun' WHEN 'power' THEN 'Power' WHEN 'rf_hardware' THEN 'RF hardware' WHEN 'software' THEN 'Software' ELSE category END AS category_label, round(100 * count_if(precursor = 'early warning ignored') / count(*), 1) AS pct_early_warning_ignored, count(*) AS tickets ",
        "FROM trouble_ticket_insights ",
        "GROUP BY 1 HAVING count_if(precursor = 'early warning ignored') > 0 ",
        "ORDER BY pct_early_warning_ignored DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "duplicates",
      "displayName": "duplicates",
      "queryLines": [
        "SELECT date_trunc('MONTH', opened_ts) AS month, sum(duplicate_tickets_opened) AS duplicate_tickets, count(*) AS tickets FROM trouble_tickets ",
        "WHERE opened_ts < DATE'2026-07-01' GROUP BY 1\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "kpi_daily",
      "displayName": "kpi daily",
      "queryLines": [
        "SELECT h.day, h.sites_down, h.alarms, COALESCE(i.incidents,0) AS incidents, COALESCE(i.silent_degradations,0) AS silent_degradations\nFROM (\n  SELECT date_trunc('DAY', ts) AS day, max(sites_down) AS sites_down, sum(alarms_raised) AS alarms\n  FROM gold_network_hourly GROUP BY 1\n) h\nLEFT JOIN (\n  SELECT date_trunc('DAY', detected_ts) AS day, count(*) AS incidents, count_if(incident_type = 'kpi_anomaly') AS silent_degradations\n  FROM noc_incidents GROUP BY 1\n) i ON h.day = i.day\nORDER BY h.day"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "pages": [
    {
      "name": "noc",
      "displayName": "Network Operations",
      "layout": [
        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "title",
            "multilineTextboxSpec": {
              "lines": [
                "# Halcyon Wireless — Network Operations\n",
                "\n",
                "**The story** — this morning at **05:57** a contractor cut the fiber of aggregation router **AGG-DEN-04**; the secondary path failed under load and the router isolated, taking **64 of its 68 cell sites** offline (**~100K subscribers**). One root cause sits behind **hundreds** of alarms.\n",
                "\n",
                "**What to see** — the KPI counters carry the live network state with a 4-week sparkline · the storm timeline shows the cliff the instant the router isolated · the topology bar proves it is **one** router, not a scattered outage · the KPI-anomaly model (bottom-left table) also flags a sector **degrading for three weeks that never raised an alarm**."
              ]
            }
          },
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "width": 6,
            "height": 4
          }
        },
